From d4cabac0d84671e8f54e3474548d25bddf735c66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Pratap Sidhu <pratapkevin8@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:57:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [NUI] Skeleton injection from a local pipe

--nui_skeleton_inject=pipe:<name> serves \.\pipe\<name> and injects
the poses another local process writes into it: one fixed-size
SkeletonPipeRecord per tracker frame (magic XNUISKL1, tracking id, 20
joints in the title's sensor space with their tracking states, and an
optional floor plane). Local clients only, one writer at a time,
offered again when the writer leaves.

Records are checked before use: a body must have a tracking id and
finite joints in front of the sensor, joint states must be ones the
runtime knows, a floor must have a unit normal. A record that fails is
dropped whole. The newest valid record is injected while it is under
250 ms old; with none fresh, frames go to the title as its tracker made
them, and the log says when that starts and stops. A record without a
body empties the slots. Its floor plane replaces the tracker's fit.

Tested: xenia-nui-tests pass (88 cases, 37279 assertions; 2 new for
the record reader). Kinect Adventures (4D5308ED) with --nui=pipe and
synth_depth.py --live replaying recorded frames into both pipes: the
writer connected, injection took poses from runtime frame 8, and every
logged play frame carried the pipe's body with one id and its floor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
